Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns & their potential use  
Match.home_team_api_id : identify the home‑side team in each match  
Match.away_team_api_id : identify the away‑side team in each match  
Match.home_team_goal    : number of goals scored by the home team – used to decide a home win  
Match.away_team_goal    : number of goals scored by the away team – used to decide an away win  
Team.team_api_id        : primary key that links a team to the Match table  
Team.team_long_name     : readable team name to show in the final result  
Main conditions  
• Home win  : Match.home_team_goal  > Match.away_team_goal  
• Away win  : Match.away_team_goal  > Match.home_team_goal  


Below are ten exploratory queries (each limited to 20 rows) that gradually build up to the final answer.  
Every query is different and uses DISTINCT where reasonable.

```sql
-- 1) List a sample of all teams with their readable names
SELECT DISTINCT "team_api_id",
       "team_long_name"
FROM   "Team"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Show distinct home‑side team IDs that ever appeared in the Match table
SELECT DISTINCT "home_team_api_id"
FROM   "Match"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Show distinct away‑side team IDs that ever appeared in the Match table
SELECT DISTINCT "away_team_api_id"
FROM   "Match"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Sample of home‑team winners (IDs only)
SELECT DISTINCT "home_team_api_id"
FROM   "Match"
WHERE  "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Sample of away‑team winners (IDs only)
SELECT DISTINCT "away_team_api_id"
FROM   "Match"
WHERE  "away_team_goal" > "home_team_goal"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Home‑team winners joined with their names
SELECT DISTINCT m."home_team_api_id",
       t."team_long_name"
FROM   "Match" AS m
JOIN   "Team"  AS t
       ON m."home_team_api_id" = t."team_api_id"
WHERE  m."home_team_goal" > m."away_team_goal"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Away‑team winners joined with their names
SELECT DISTINCT m."away_team_api_id",
       t."team_long_name"
FROM   "Match" AS m
JOIN   "Team"  AS t
       ON m."away_team_api_id" = t."team_api_id"
WHERE  m."away_team_goal" > m."home_team_goal"
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Count total wins per team (IDs only, highest 20)
SELECT w."team_api_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "wins"
FROM   (
        SELECT "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id"
        FROM   "Match"
        WHERE  "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal"
        UNION ALL
        SELECT "away_team_api_id"
        FROM   "Match"
        WHERE  "away_team_goal" > "home_team_goal"
       ) AS w
GROUP  BY w."team_api_id"
ORDER  BY "wins" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same as #8 but with readable team names
SELECT t."team_long_name",
       w."wins"
FROM   (
        SELECT w."team_api_id",
               COUNT(*) AS "wins"
        FROM   (
                SELECT "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id"
                FROM   "Match"
                WHERE  "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal"
                UNION ALL
                SELECT "away_team_api_id"
                FROM   "Match"
                WHERE  "away_team_goal" > "home_team_goal"
               ) AS w
        GROUP BY w."team_api_id"
       ) AS w
JOIN   "Team" AS t
       ON w."team_api_id" = t."team_api_id"
ORDER  BY w."wins" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER – Top‑10 teams with the most wins in the entire dataset
SELECT t."team_long_name"  AS "Team",
       w."wins"            AS "Total_Wins"
FROM  (
       SELECT w."team_api_id",
              COUNT(*) AS "wins"
       FROM  (
              SELECT "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id"
              FROM   "Match"
              WHERE  "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal"
              UNION ALL
              SELECT "away_team_api_id"
              FROM   "Match"
              WHERE  "away_team_goal" > "home_team_goal"
             ) AS w
       GROUP BY w."team_api_id"
      ) AS w
JOIN  "Team" AS t
      ON w."team_api_id" = t."team_api_id"
ORDER BY w."wins" DESC
LIMIT 10;
```
